    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm a freelance designer and i'm trying to clean up my quickbooks for the year. i just bought a really expensive ergonomic chair for my home studio setup. do i categorize that as a business expense or is it a personal draw? i'm a bit confused about how the irs views home office equipment.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For tax purposes, presumably when you file your taxes and items purchased for your home office can qualify as a business expense if it enhances your ability to perform your work, and depending on the nature of the expense and where it was purchased. To claim it as a business expense (also known as a deductible expense), you need to meet certain IRS requirements, such as using the home office exclusively and regularly for conducting business, and it must be ordinary and necessary for your freelance work. However, since it's a home studio and not a typical office, you may need to keep detailed records to justify the claim. It is recommended to keep the receipts and any other evidence of home office business expenses and consult with a tax professional to ensure you're following the IRS guidelines correctly.",
      "source": "target",
